{"id": "4ae2e2a6-9792-43ac-a684-a849ff03f14c", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:29:26.235221", "source": "user", "parent_id": "f5436dd7-0ae7-476f-abdd-feb1131cb55d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"अभी सिर्फ़ इनपुट inspection और एक proposed approach चाहिए — पूरा solution अभी मत दो। ये design-only टास्क है, experiment चलाना नहीं है; deliverable एक ठोस experiment design है (rationale, controls, analysis plan, feasibility के साथ)।\\n\\nचरण 1 — Repository inspection (/workspace): zero bubble pipeline parallelism की 1F1B, 1F1B-I, ZB-1p, ZB-2p implementations ढूँढो। बताओ कि ये methods codebase में कहाँ हैं, microbatch count का bubble structure से क्या relation है (theoretically — ZB-1p bubble कितने microbatches पर गायब होता है, ZB-2p क्यों फ्यू stable रहता है), और कोई मौजूदा benchmark script/launch configs हैं या नहीं।\\n\\nचरण 2 — Proposed approach: ये बताओ कि experiment कैसे structure करोगे — (a) कौन-से variables hold करोगे (pipeline depth, layer config/model, total batch size, sequence length, hardware/device topology, precision), (b) कौन-सा independent variable vary करोगे (number of microbatches — कौन-से levels, क्यों), (c) throughput metric क्या लोगे (samples/sec, tokens/sec, या MFU), (d) controls और repeats, (e) analysis plan (per-method मोनोटोनिक trend की जाँच, ZB-2p के flat/high-throughput profile की तुलना बाकी methods से)।\\n\\nचरण 3 — Feasibility & assumptions: GPUs उपलब्ध नहीं हैं, इसलिए बताओ कि ये design बिना execution के कैसे feasible है (जैसे analytical bubble-throughput computation, या भविष्य के GPU run के लिए spec), और जो चीज़ें ज़रूरी हैं उन्हें assumption के तौर पर list करो — मसलन कौन-सा model/architecture assume करना है, क्या 1F1B baseline control के तौर पर चाहिए, runtime budget, repeats की संख्या। इन्हें 'assumption' मार्क करो, confirmed fact मत समझो।\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the throughput for methods 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches? (Note: These methods are implemented as part of the zero bubble pipeline parallelism strategies in this repository, which aim to reduce pipeline bubbles and maintain high throughput.)\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
